*> Implementation test (002-lane-mobsfull-h5; docs/protocol/20 section 6.1 Creeper, powered): lightning (STDMOB-POWER) makes only a creeper powered (variant 1,
*> metadata 17 boolean); a powered creeper explodes with power 6, so a player 6.5 blocks away is hurt while a plain creeper (power 3, 2R = 6) leaves it unhurt.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-20-6-1.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY BRWORLD.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CREEPER-TYPE        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZOMBIE-TYPE         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-M                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-X0                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-STOP                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-POWERED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CASE                PIC X(100).
 01 WS-EXP                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OBS                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-VIEW BASED.
    05 WS-BYTE             PIC X OCCURS 64 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "MS-TEST-OPEN" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     MOVE "minecraft:creeper" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-CREEPER-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE "minecraft:zombie" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-ZOMBIE-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-X
     MOVE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Y
     MOVE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-Z
     COMPUTE WS-X0 = WS-X + 6.5
*>   A zombie is not powered by lightning.
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-ZOMBIE-TYPE WS-X0 WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-ROW
     CALL "STDMOB-POWER" USING WS-ROW WS-POWERED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: lightning does not power a zombie" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-EXP
     COMPUTE WS-OBS = WS-POWERED + EN-VARIANT(WS-ROW)
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-ROW
*>   A plain creeper at the fuse: power 3 does not reach 6.5 blocks.
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-CREEPER-TYPE WS-X0 WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-ROW
     CALL "STDMOB-INDEX" USING WS-CREEPER-TYPE WS-M
     MOVE PL-ENTITY-ID(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-TARGET-ID(WS-ROW)
     MOVE WS-PLAYER TO EN-TARGET(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 29 TO EN-SWELL(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 20 TO PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HURT-COOLDOWN(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-ROW WS-M WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: a plain creeper explodes at the fuse" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-EXP
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: power 3 leaves a player 6.5 blocks away unhurt" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 20 TO WS-EXP
     MOVE PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-OBS
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
*>   A powered creeper: variant 1, power 6.
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-CREEPER-TYPE WS-X0 WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-ROW
     CALL "STDMOB-POWER" USING WS-ROW WS-POWERED
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: lightning powers a creeper" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 11 TO WS-EXP
     COMPUTE WS-OBS = WS-POWERED * 10 + EN-VARIANT(WS-ROW)
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "STDMOB-VARIANT-BUILD" USING WS-ROW PB-BUFFER
     SET ADDRESS OF WS-VIEW TO PB-ADDR
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: the powered flag is Set Entity Data index 17" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-EXP
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OBS
     IF PB-LENGTH > 5 AND WS-BYTE(1) = X"65"
         MOVE 1 TO WS-OBS
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     MOVE PL-ENTITY-ID(WS-PLAYER) TO EN-TARGET-ID(WS-ROW)
     MOVE WS-PLAYER TO EN-TARGET(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 29 TO EN-SWELL(WS-ROW)
     MOVE 20 TO PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE 0 TO PL-HURT-COOLDOWN(WS-PLAYER)
     CALL "STDMOB-SWELL" USING WS-ROW WS-M WS-STOP
     MOVE "acceptance US15 20§6.1 Creeper: power 6 hurts a player 6.5 blocks away" TO WS-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-EXP
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OBS
     IF PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER) < 20
         MOVE 1 TO WS-OBS
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-CHK" USING WS-CASE WS-EXP WS-OBS
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-20-6-1.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CHK.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-CASE                 PIC X(100).
 01 L-EXPECTED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-OBSERVED             BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-CASE L-EXPECTED L-OBSERVED.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE L-CASE TO TL-CASE
     MOVE L-EXPECTED TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE L-OBSERVED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CHK.
 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY MOBSPTEST.
